# Topic: Compile Luau C++ static libraries in parallel
#
# What it does: configures all Luau static libraries into per-library output
# subfolders and compiles them concurrently inside std::thread::scope (sharing
# cc's process-wide Cargo jobserver), then moves each static archive back into
# build_dir in deterministic order.
#
# Why upstream lacks it: upstream luau0-src compiles ten static libraries one
# after another, leaving cores idle at nine inter-library tail-latency barriers
# (and on small 1-3 file libraries) during clean and uncached builds.
